{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1363788-question-about-mage-the-awakening-and-the-archmage-myrddin-merlin","id":1363788,"title":"Question about Mage: the Awakening and the Archmage Myrddin/Merlin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-28T07:42:27-08:00","id":1363788,"title":"Question about Mage: the Awakening and the Archmage Myrddin/Merlin?","content":"I just finished reading the part in Dark Eras 2 about Arthur's Britannia and I couldn't find anything about how the Archmage Myrddin (Dark Eras 2 calls him Merlin) shatters the Dream of Camelot in order to Ascend. I read a whole thread about this on the forums. Where can I go to read the official sourcebook that talks about this topic in more detail (apparently it's not Dark Eras 2)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:29:40-08:00","id":1363805,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think there is a book that goes into it in full detail. There\u2019s been a smattering of mentions of it, in Signs of Sorcery is one place, I\u2019m pretty sure Imperial Mysteries is another. There might be a few others I\u2019m not remembering. Most of our information comes from comments from Dave I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:59:36-08:00","id":1363819,"title":"","content":"Mage Camelot was one of the two contenders for the first Dark Era's Mage setting, the other being Alexandrian Mage. At the time, Dave decided the founding of the Orders during the Alexandrian period was more evocative of the direction Mage was going for the Second Edition and settled on that, but figured it might come up in another book. As far as I know, he was not contacted about the Camelot in Dark Eras 2, which went the direction you see there-which works out, because Mage Camelot is probably better presented in a book handling Mage. The last major idea was that it might come in a future book where it would fit in. Who knows where it sits with the current development cycle. I don't imagine it's going to be left alone though.<br /> <br /> If you go up to search, click &quot;Search in Mage the Awakening only&quot; and make your keyword Camelot, you'll find a whole bunch of stuff where it's been discussed, including Dave Brookshaw's comments and ideas on it, but for ease of access, here's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot\">the thread</a> where it first came up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:05:41-08:00","id":1363821,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so the Camelot story is spread out across the whole game line - you're looking for one-page (often just one-paragraph) mentions in the first edition Mage corebook, Tome of the Watchtowers, Tome of the Mysteries, Astral Realms, Silver Ladder, Left Hand Path, Imperial Mysteries, the second edition corebook, and Signs of Sorcery. So far.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T12:56:20-08:00","id":1363843,"title":"","content":"Thank you!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}